  {
   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Properties of standard deviation"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "S.D. is independent of change of origin but not of scale: if $y = (x - A)/h$ then $\\sigma_x = |h|\\,\\sigma_y$. The S.D. of a constant is zero. For a frequency distribution use $\\sigma^2 = \\sum f x^2/N - \\bar{x}^2$, with class mid-points as x.",
    "kn": "ಮಾನಕ ವಿಚಲನೆ ಮೂಲ ಬದಲಾವಣೆಯಿಂದ ಸ್ವತಂತ್ರ, ಆದರೆ ಮಾಪನ ಬದಲಾವಣೆಯಿಂದ ಸ್ವತಂತ್ರವಲ್ಲ: y = (x − A)/h ಆದರೆ σₓ = |h|σᵧ. ಸ್ಥಿರಾಂಕದ ಮಾನಕ ವಿಚಲನೆ ಶೂನ್ಯ."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "Adding a constant: σ unchanged"
    },
    {
     "en": "Multiplying by k: σ becomes |k|σ"
    },
    {
     "en": "S.D. of a constant = 0"
    }
   ],
   "formula": "\\sigma_x = |h|\\,\\sigma_y \\quad \\text{where } y = \\frac{x - A}{h}",
   "narration": {
    "en": "S.D. is independent of change of origin but not of scale: if y = (x - A)/h then \\sigma_x = |h|\\,\\sigma_y. The S.D. of a constant is zero. For a frequency distribution use \\sigma^2 = \\sum f x^2/N - \\bar{x}^2, with class mid-points as x.",
